# CARD-0604 D-17 / G-35: the only sudo grant that exists inside the persistent server2 runner.
#
# uid 1654 (the session runner and every session it holds) may run exactly the two root-owned
# custody helpers and nothing else. There is no ALL command, no second user, no second target
# uid and no password prompt to answer. This file is CONTAINER-internal: it constrains the
# uid-1654 test/mutation process inside an already-privileged container and has nothing to do
# with server2's own host sudoers.
#
# Note for anyone widening this: a tracked child cannot use it anyway. antiphon-custody-enter
# execs the child under PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS, which makes sudo -- and every other setuid binary
# -- inert for the whole descendant tree. Only the observing pty-host, which lives outside the
# tree, can call these.
#
# ASCII only. Installed 0440 root:root; `visudo -c` runs at image build time.

Defaults:#1654 env_reset
# The shim must be reached by exec, not by a forked sudo: the pid Porta spawned has to be the
# pid that ends up inside the cgroup, and it must keep the pty it was given. sudo 1.9.14+ turns
# use_pty on by default, which would put the tracked child behind a second pty; a PAM session
# would make sudo fork so it can close that session afterwards. Both are turned off for this one
# grant so `sudo -n antiphon-custody-enter ...` is a plain exec.
Defaults:#1654 !use_pty
Defaults:#1654 !pam_session

#1654 ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/antiphon-custody-enter, /usr/local/bin/antiphon-custody-kill
